SUMMARY (for orientation only; the EULA is binding)
===================================================

Free use:
  Free of charge for as long as your organization reaches NONE of these
  three thresholds:

    (a) one hundred (100) employees,
    (b) ten million Euro (EUR 10,000,000) annual turnover,
    (c) twenty-one (21) developers.

  "Organization" includes linked enterprises under common control: a
  subsidiary is counted together with its group. A minority participation
  without control does not by itself join two organizations. See EULA
  sections 4.2 / 14.2 for the complete definitions.

Always free, regardless of the thresholds:
  - Natural persons, for private, hobby or educational purposes.
  - Accredited educational institutions, for teaching, learning and
    non-commercial research (not for contract research).
  - Work you do for clients: the thresholds measure YOUR organization
    only. The size of your client does not matter, including when you
    work on their premises.

Commercial license required:
  - If your organization reaches or exceeds even one threshold, a
    ninety-day transition period begins. Use stays free of charge during
    that period; a commercial license is required to continue afterwards.
  - The ninety days are a contractual period only. The software starts no
    timer, sends no threshold or deadline data, blocks no feature and does
    not technically stop working when the period ends.
  - Commercial licenses start at EUR 25 per licensed developer per
    month. Price and scope may depend on licensed users, requested
    support and response scope, and agreed priority or delivery
    commitments for improvement requests.
  - A written agreement may include support with defined response and
    security-fix targets (for example, answers within two business days
    and fixes for confirmed vulnerabilities within ten business days),
    version maintenance, prioritized general product improvements, and
    source-code review under NDA. Payment alone creates no unstated SLA,
    warranty or implementation promise.
  - Customer code is never collected or used for improvement automatically.
    Any examination requires material or access deliberately provided by
    the customer and a separate agreement on scope and confidentiality.

No technical license enforcement:
  - No license server, activation token, watermarking or phone-home.
  - The MCP server may record local operational data about tool calls for
    usage_report and the local MCP Usage view. This is not license telemetry
    and never leaves the machine.

Donations:
  - Voluntary and welcome (e.g., https://github.com/sponsors/gregordadera),
    but they are a separate matter. A donation does NOT replace a
    commercial license where one is required.

Restrictions:
  - No reverse engineering, decompilation, or disassembly, except as
    permitted by mandatory applicable law (German Copyright Act
    sections 69d / 69e for interoperability).
  - No removal or alteration of copyright notices, trademarks, or
    version information.
  - No redistribution, modification, repackaging, re-branding or resale of
    the AICB software itself.
  - No bundling of the AICB binaries into another product and no hosted or
    shared AICB service for direct third-party use without written permission.
  - No competing products based on this software.

Intended integration and outputs:
  - Connecting AICB to MCP clients, agent harnesses, scripts, build systems
    and CI/CD through its documented interfaces is permitted.
  - Consultants may use AICB internally while serving clients; the client
    does not receive a hosted AICB service merely because its code is analyzed.
  - You retain all rights in your source code. AICB acquires no rights merely
    by analyzing it locally.
  - Generated context, exports, .aicb.json sidecars and files installed by
    aicb init may be used, adapted, versioned and shared, subject to rights in
    their underlying source and third-party content.
  - Bundled third-party components remain governed by the licenses listed in
    THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.

Trademarks:
  - "AIContextBuilder" and "AIContextBuilder for .NET" are unregistered
    product names used by Gregor Dadera. Any protection arises under the
    applicable name and trademark law; no registration is claimed.

Warranty and liability:
  - Software is provided "as is", without warranty.
  - Liability limited per EULA sections 9 / 19 (German law: unlimited for
    intent and gross negligence; limited to typical foreseeable damage
    for ordinary negligence in case of breach of cardinal duties).

Governing law:
  - German law applies. Exclusive jurisdiction at the domicile of the
    licensor (Gregor Dadera) for merchants and legal entities; statutory
